Apache 2.0 packages:

  - @lloyal-labs/channel-verify       (packages/channel-verify)

@lloyal-labs/channel-verify is Apache 2.0 by design, not by omission: it is
the public half of an asymmetric signing scheme (signature verification
only — it holds no private key and cannot mint trust), and any client that
wishes to verify the channel must be free to do so. It carries no runtime
dependency on the FSL runtime stack and no native binary.

Each package ships its own LICENSE file. The native stack carries separate
notices for liblloyal and third-party dependencies such as llama.cpp.

